# NeSPReSO project context

Read [`HANDOFF.md`](../../HANDOFF.md) for current status.

## What this is

Batch PyTorch training: surface inputs → PCA latent → T/S profiles. Tags: `isas20` (HDF5 patches), `argo_v2` (v2 pickle). No HTTP API, no database.

## Trust boundaries

- `pickle.load` / `torch.load` on caches and checkpoints — only trusted paths on shared FS.
- `parse_config.init_obj` + `getattr` — config `type` fields select classes; validate at boundary.
- `validate_config()` in `parse_config.py` — extend here, don't add parallel config layers.

## Eval

- Within-tag: `eval_run.py` + matching cache/checkpoint.
- Cross-tag: `eval_matched.py` only — never headline ISAS vs ARGO raw RMSE side by side.

## Bottleneck

`CombinedPCALoss` PCA inverse (`model/loss.py`) dominates ARGO (1801 levels). MLP forward is tiny; GoM GPU opts rarely help.

## Checks

After non-trivial changes: `srun --ntasks=1 --cpus-per-task=8 python3 selfcheck.py`
